quests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":75932.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1610.0,"requests":4}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Reconcile the 'stays quiet on review-bot hosts' claim with the mechanism: either move the actual-pass stamping into run_gc (so any successful pass — resident thread OR triggered child — refreshes <store>/gc/last-pass.stamp, keeping the stamp-only-when-skipped-is-None discipline intact and giving the resident janitor a real fresh clock) OR drop the 'stays quiet' claim and state that review-bot hosts spawn a harmless child that degrades to skipped=\"locked\".","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'because its passes go through the same run_gc, hosts where it runs simply see fresh passes and the op-linked trigger stays quiet'","janitor.py:508-515 _loop calls run_gc(config=cfg) directly with no last-pass.stamp write","Plan places stamping in the child: 'the child stamps last-pass.stamp only when run_gc ran (skipped is None)' — run_gc itself does not stamp","run_gc (janitor.py:321-365) returns GcResult and takes only <store>/gc/lock flock; it has no knowledge of <store>/gc/last-pass.stamp"],"finding":"The plan asserts the op-linked trigger 'stays quiet' on a review-bot host because the resident janitor's passes 'go through the same run_gc' and the host 'sees fresh passes', but the stamping of last-pass.stamp is placed in the trigger's detached child (run_detached), not in run_gc, and the resident janitor (start_background_janitor) calls run_gc(config=cfg) directly without ever writing last-pass.stamp. Therefore a review-bot host's stamp stays stale/missing and the trigger will spawn a redundant detached child on every attested gate resolution (harmless via single-flight/gc-flock -> skipped=\"locked\", but not 'quiet' as claimed).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd1bc6f85074c51a9","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section, final bullet ('The stamp records only an actual pass'); AC line 4 ('the resident janitor is not regressed')","norm_id":"ne23b07b4052cd1a9","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A review-bot host resolving attested gates: each resolution finds a stale stamp (resident janitor never refreshed it) and spawns a detached child that immediately loses the gc flock/worker.lock -> skipped=\"locked\", never stamps -> the next gate resolution repeats the spawn."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Move the stamp write into run_gc itself, gated on skipped is None, so both the resident janitor loop and the detached child refresh last-pass.stamp on every real pass — preserving the stand-aside/locked no-stamp rule while making the 'fresh passes -> trigger stays quiet' claim actually hold.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Scope AC 1 to POSIX hosts (or state the Windows reclamation story) so the win32 no-op does not leave the acceptance criterion overclaiming for a supported platform.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.57,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Detached child (_spawn_detached_gc ...): ... POSIX-only v1 (win32 no-op, exactly like compact_trigger and enrich_drain).'","AC 1: 'A host that runs attested gates WITHOUT the review-bot server reclaims its snapshot store'","Windows is a named cell of the platform/venue matrix; a Windows workstation without the review-bot server would never reclaim, so its store grows unbounded (the 47 GiB failure mode)."],"finding":"The reclamation mechanism is POSIX-only v1 with a win32 no-op, but Acceptance Criterion 1 states unqualified that 'A host that runs attested gates WITHOUT the review-bot server reclaims its snapshot store.' On a Windows developer workstation (a first-class supported platform) running `rebar review-plan`/`review-code` without the review-bot server, the win32 no-op means the detached GC is never spawned, so the snapshot store accumulates unbounded exactly as in the motivating bug — the AC is false there.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe4c288b2346e07db","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Detached child' bullet ('POSIX-only v1 (win32 no-op ...)') and AC line 1","norm_id":"n18ef7bba062b1609","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Windows workstation, no review-bot server: gate resolution invokes maybe_gc → win32 no-op → no spawn → store never reclaimed → same unbounded growth the ticket is fixing.","Windows CI runner resolving attested gates: store on the runner accumulates across builds with no reclamation path."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Qualify AC 1 as 'a POSIX host that runs attested gates WITHOUT the review-bot server reclaims its snapshot store' and add a note in docs/scope that Windows reclamation on non-review-bot hosts is deferred (matching compact_trigger/enrich_drain), or confirm the review-bot resident janitor still covers Windows review-bot hosts.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"faa96e8806071c4